        "answer": "# Newton's Second Law of Motion\n\nNewton's Second Law of Motion relates the net external force acting on a body to its acceleration. It states that the rate of change of momentum of an object is proportional to the applied force and takes place in the direction of the force.\n\nThe mathematical formulation is:\n$F = ma$\n\nWhere:\n*   **F** = net external force\n*   **m** = mass of the body\n*   **a** = acceleration of the body\n\nThis means that a greater force is required to produce a larger acceleration for a given mass, or to accelerate a larger mass at the same rate. \n\n**📘 Source:** NCERT Class 11 Physics • Newton Second Law"
